  "notes": "The reference half is a HEADLESS COMMAND capture \u2014 no display, no pointer injection, no gesture \u2014 so it carries none of the drag-transport caveats. The vibe3d half is measured live from this tree at generation time, so `vibe3d_current` is a regression pin on our own behaviour, not a transcription. Both cells are open meshes; the degenerate remnant is the object of study, so the face/edge counts carry the finding and are asserted on both sides. The remnants are real document state now, not a transient: they survive .v3d save/load, undo/redo and the GPU upload \u2014 two one-sided drops in the .v3d READER had to be removed for that (an arity floor of 3, and a flat refusal to open a mesh with no polygons at all)."
